        "text": "# Object\n\nAn **object** is a bundle of related information in JavaScript, stored as name-value pairs called *properties*. \n\nIt lets you represent a real-world thing (like a backpack or dessert) in code.\n\nFor example, a backback object might have properties such as `name: \"backpack\"`, `color: \"blue\"`, and `size: 30`.",
